  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY NIGHT THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 235 PM CDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nThursday...Latest ensemble upper ridge placement and thermal \ngradient projections suggest another hot day of headline worthy \nheat, but also some upper ridge retrograde may be enough to allow \nfor some convection to spill further southeast and possibly impact \nportions of the local fcst area especially Thu night into Friday \nmorning. But that being said, some of the longer range CAMs such as \nthe latest RRFS suggest bulk of the convection this day to occur to \nthe north and east of the CWA. If organized storms/ clusters do \nmanage to make it down this way, severe weather and damaging winds \nwould be probable.\n\nFriday...Depending on the potential for more storms down our way or \nat least convective debris and storm outflow, like the previous shift \nmentioned, this day may need an eventual heat headline. And if it \ndoes, the several days of high heat in a row rule may foster the \nneed for an upgrade to an Extreme Heat Warning.\n\nA look ahead to the upcoming weekend: Saturday could be a \ncontinuation of the hot humid weather and possible need of heat \nheadlines, depending on storms and cloud debris. But then the heat \nmay decrease by Sunday if we can get a backdoor style cool front \nfrom ridging acrs the western GRT LKS. This may be temporary with \nensemble signs in the medium range runs of the heat dome trying to \nreestablish from the west and back acrs the region by mid next week.",
